## What changed

- `src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts` (new): `writeMuseDelivery(options): Promise<StorytimeManifest>`
  and the types `MuseApprovalEntry`, `MuseApprovalList`, `MuseDeliveryOptions`.
- `src/storytime/book-pictures.ts`: `rowCaptureJob` is exported (one word). The CLI has a new
  `deliver` command.

The writer reuses `assembleManifest` (it builds the batch hashes with `batchSha256` and
`BATCH_HASH_ALGORITHM`), `planPictureRow`, `inspectLineArtPng`, `priceForProvider`,
`PICTURE_RUBRIC_VERSION`, and `rowCaptureJob`. It runs every check before the first write, copies
the print files byte for byte, writes `manifest.json` last, refuses a different manifest or a
different file under a list name, and gives the same bytes on a second run. It maps only the Kimi
review (`reviews.kimi`) and a named person review from the approval entry.

CLI line:
`node --import tsx scripts/storytime-book-pictures.ts deliver --list <pictures.json> --approvals <approved.json> --muse <muse folder> --delivery <delivery folder>`.
It is read only, offline, and uses no key. A smoke run on the real row `l2-w01-check-row-bus`
(output under `/tmp`) exited 0 with 1 job and 2 batches (`w01/color`, `w01/lineart`).

